**Verdict: REJECT** (as a plan ready to implement). Three of the five requested properties hold. One is restored in name only, one has regressed, and the plan's central premise, named variables in the semantic layer, is not in the architecture document it cites. `plan.md` is the migration plan, `cat.md` is `docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`, `idx.cljc` is `src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc`, `tx.cljc` is `src/cljc/dao/space/transact.cljc`.

## Status of the five requested properties

| Requested property | Status |
|---|---|
| 1. Projection before emission | **Partially addressed.** The walker reading a map AST from a stream topic is now an owner ruling (commit fbbab7d, cat.md:912). The Map AST Indexer into `dao.space` was not removed and remains a defect (finding 2). The doc itself now contradicts the ruling at cat.md:158-162 (finding 5). |
| 2. Staged encoder output | **Named, not specified.** plan.md:52 says "staged-output" and nothing else. No load/run split, no `:next` cursor, no append order (finding 4). |
| 3. Transactor for the datom ledger, `:resolved` index | **Passed.** Verified against code: `transact!` stamps one `t` and appends one `{:dao.space/transaction {:t :datoms}}` record (`transactor.cljc:134-155`, `:231-254`); a `:resolved` session flattens that record and rejects tempids (`idx.cljc:376-410`, `:666-674`, `:869-877`); unique-identity upsert exists only in the transactor (`tx.cljc:302-325`). S2 now has one writer. Residual schema gap in finding 3. |
| 4. Occurrence keys with medium, batch, j | **Regressed.** v2 carried `[:yin.occ/origin :yin.occ/root :yin.occ/path]`; v3 (plan.md:55) carries only the origin `[medium batch j]`, which is an origin, not an occurrence key (cat.md:402-413). `medium` and `batch` remain unnamed (finding 3). |
| 5. Batch envelope with `:yin/declarations` and `:yin/harvest` | **Passed.** plan.md:54 lists all four keys. Minor completion gap in finding 8. |

